From 65f80f4ff540666a8861f36c52f8b6eec0740b9c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 05:12:09 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(compression): an answered request is not "in
 flight" during a later notice turn
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A mid-turn compaction of a Kanban-notice turn restated a human request answered an hour
earlier as "STILL IN PROGRESS — this is the active request"; the agent re-answered it
(~25 API calls at 180-220k input tokens) while queued notices waited.

_find_inflight_user_task took the newest actionable human row and only checked the
transcript END for a completed reply. Notice rows (kanban_notice, internal_notification,
process_complete, async_delegation_complete) are never actionable, so a notice-started turn
has no visible trigger, and a mid-turn compaction always ends on a tool result.

A request is now in flight only while its turn has not ended: a completed assistant reply
followed by a turn-starting notice row ends it (agent/context_compressor_turns.py).
Same-turn rows (auto_continue, steer, scaffolding, unknown kinds) do not. Replay/merge
layout unchanged. The facade's stale image-anchor comment in _find_inflight_user_task
(copied from the image stripper) is removed to offset the FILE_LINES cap.

Proof: tests/agent/test_inflight_turn_ended_by_notice.py: 9 fail on the base, 19 pass
after (incl. the observed 04:21 transcript shape from state.db and an end-to-end compress()).
Mutants on every added condition killed (10/10). 109 compressor test files green locally.
